hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2850","Narrated to us Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us Sufyan, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Usamah ibn Zayd (RA), who said:\n\nWe dismounted with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from 'Arafat. When he reached the valley where the commanders usually camped, he urinated, then performed wudu'. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the prayer is now!\" He replied, \"The prayer is ahead of you.\"\n\nWhen he reached al-Jam' (Muzdalifah), he gave the adhan and iqamah, then prayed Maghrib. He did not let the people disperse until he established the iqamah and prayed 'Isha'.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
